Ok, straight from the source:

I'm not going into angering gods or converting altars or self nor into 
any other things like that. So my basic assumption is that you are 
sacrifying a normal creature's corpse (undead and cross-aligned unicorns 
are ok, your own race isn't) on a coaligned altar.

The difficulty and type of monster only affects your standing with your 
god. When you've got the reconciliation message or no message at all you 
are ready to get an artifact gift. As long as your god is angry you 
cannot get the reconciliation message so angry gods never give artifacts.

If you are ready to get an artifact the following conditions have to be 
satisfied before you can get it:

1. Your level is higher than 2.
2. Your luck is not negative.
3. A random number from 0 to nine plus two times the number of already 
got artifact gifts times the number of created artifacts is 0.

The latter in simplified terms, 0 in the range:

0..9 if you haven't got any artifact gift.
0..9+2*n^2 when the only artifacts in the game has been gifts where n is 
the number of such gifts.
0..9+2*n*(n+m) where n is number of artifact gifts and m is the number 
of other artifacts.

So even if there are artifacts genereated in the game this chance of 
getting an artifact gift is 1 in 10.

Last catch is that if all generable artifacts have been generated then 
you don't get any.

Otherwise you get what is generated. What is generated is a separate 
discussion.

So, level higher than 2, god reconciliated (= you can pray, implies god 
not angry), luck not negative => 1 in 10 chance that you get your first 
gift, 1 in 12 to get the second and 1 in 28 to get the third (4th 1/42, 
5th 1/60 etc.) (As long as no other artifacts are generated while you 
are sacrificing.)

If you have done the quest, made the Sting and the Orcrist, wished for 
the Eyes or the Eye (depending if you are a wizard or a monk), found the 
Snickersnee in a shop, but haven't got any gift artifact the chance is 1 
in 10 that you get your first gift, 1 in 22 to get the second and 1 in 
38 to get the third (4th 1/58, 5th 1/82 etc.) (As long as no other 
artifacts are generated while you are sacrificing.)

Let us consider a very unlikely situation where all quest artifacts are 
generated (through quest, bones or wishes), the Sting and the Orcrists 
are named and all other, but one, artifacts are generated as gifts (with 
nice usage of the Helm of Opposite Alignment). What is the chance to get 
the one remaining artifact through sacrifice? What about wish?

There is 20 non-quest artifacts, the Sting And the Orcrist are in these.
There is 13 quest artifacts (13 roles ABCHKMPRaRoSTVW).

So the chance on sacrifice is 1 in 10 plus 2 times all but one (42) 
times gifts (17) which is 1/1438.

A whish on the other hand is 1 in 42, But you can sacrifise all night 
long but wishes are far between.

